# annotatoR Deploy & Smoke Test

## Critical Fact

The live Shiny service loads the **installed R package**, not the repo's
`inst/app/app.R` directly:

```
service  ──loads──▶  library(annotatoR)
                         │
                         └──▶  /home/wschulz/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/4.5/annotatoR/app/app.R
```

Editing files under `projects/tools/annotatoR/repo/` has **no effect** on
the running service until both of:

1. The package is reinstalled (copies `inst/app/app.R` → installed path).
2. `annotator.service` is restarted (R loads the package at service start
   and keeps it in memory).

## Deploy Recipe

```bash
cd ~/projects/tools/annotatoR/repo
Rscript -e "devtools::install('.')"   # agent can run this (~2 min)
sudo systemctl restart annotator       # agent CANNOT run — requires user sudo
```

`sudo` is password-prompted on this host; the agent must stop after the
install step and ask the user to run the restart. Tell them the install
mtime of `/home/wschulz/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/4.5/annotatoR/app/app.R`
so they can confirm the new code landed.

## Verify Install (Before Asking for Restart)

```bash
Rscript -e 'p <- system.file("app/app.R", package = "annotatoR"); cat(format(file.info(p)$mtime), "\n")'
```

Grep the installed `app.R` for a distinctive string from your change to
confirm it actually got baked in — `devtools::install` has silently
skipped on "no change detected" in the past.

## Smoke Test Without Touching Production

Never point a test instance at the live DB. Copy it first:

```bash
mkdir -p /tmp/annotator_smoke/state
cp ~/projects/tools/annotatoR/state/annotatoR.sqlite /tmp/annotator_smoke/state/

ANNOTATOR_DB=/tmp/annotator_smoke/state/annotatoR.sqlite \
  Rscript -e 'shiny::runApp("~/projects/tools/annotatoR/repo/inst/app",
                            port = 3840L, host = "127.0.0.1",
                            launch.browser = FALSE)'
```

- Live service listens on `127.0.0.1:3839` — **always use a different port**
  (3840 is the convention) and confirm `ss -tlnp | grep :3839` shows the
  prod PID is untouched before and after your test.
- The smoke app reads `inst/app/app.R` directly, so you don't need to
  reinstall the package to test a change — reinstall is only for deploying.
- Use the browser MCP (`cursor-ide-browser`) to drive the UI; log in as
  `willschulz@github` (has 19 instruction groups, ~24k pending items —
  good coverage for progress-bar / instruction-group features).

## Rollback

If a deploy misbehaves:

```bash
cd ~/projects/tools/annotatoR/repo
git checkout <only the files you changed>     # keep unrelated uncommitted work
Rscript -e "devtools::install('.')"
sudo systemctl restart annotator              # user runs
```

Do **not** blanket `git checkout .` — the repo often has other
uncommitted local work (e.g. `NAMESPACE`, `R/tasks.R`) that isn't yours.
`git status --short` before touching anything.

## Paths Cheat Sheet

| Role | Path |
|---|---|
| Repo (source of truth) | `~/projects/tools/annotatoR/repo/` |
| Installed package | `~/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/4.5/annotatoR/` |
| Live SQLite DB | `~/projects/tools/annotatoR/state/annotatoR.sqlite` |
| Service logs | `~/projects/tools/annotatoR/state/logs/annotator.log` |
| systemd unit | `/etc/systemd/system/annotator.service` |
| Full runbook | `~/projects/tools/annotatoR/repo/RUNBOOK.md` |
